---
description: Git commit message style for Linkagram
alwaysApply: true
---

# Commit messages

Subject line:

- Imperative mood, sentence case, ends with a period.
- One line, 72 characters or fewer. No prefix, no ticket id, no emoji.
- Describe what the commit changes, not which files it touches.

```text
Add clipboard paste to the analysis screen.
Fix redirect loop detection for protocol-relative Location headers.
```

Avoid:

```text
feat(ui): add clipboard paste     # no Conventional Commits prefixes here
Added clipboard paste             # past tense, missing period
Update AnalysisScreen.kt          # names the file, not the change
fixes                             # says nothing
```

Body, expected for anything beyond a one-line change:

- Blank line after the subject, wrapped at 72 characters.
- Explain why the change is needed and what its visible effect is.
- Name the spec or ADR when the commit implements or changes one, for
  example `Implements docs/specs/002-redirect-resolution.md`.
- Do not narrate the process, list which Gradle checks ran, or add AI
  co-author trailers. AI assistance is disclosed in the pull request.

Scope:

- One logical change per commit; keep unrelated refactors separate.
- Never commit secrets or machine-specific paths such as
  `local.properties` and `.env-vars.local`.
